            <ArticleTitle>[Headache as a warning symptom].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic headache is an independent clinical picture. Headaches are to be interpreted as a warning sign from the body until this is excluded through differential diagnostics. The clarification and the initial treatment should be carried out by a neurologist to ensure sufficient diagnostic certainty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
